// EXPECT: REJECT
// ADR 0057. Operator at end of previous line with the continuation
// indented deeper: this *should* compile under the ADR's rule, but
// does not, because the lexer emits an `Indent` token before the
// continuation and `parse_unary` rejects it. That is a separate
// gap (how `Indent` interacts with expression continuations) and
// is out of scope for 0057. Retained here as a reproducer; flips
// to EXPECT: COMPILE when the Indent-in-expression issue is fixed.
proc main()
    val a := 10
    val b := 3
    val total := a +
        b
    print(total)
